## Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.binlog

## Test output
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage

## Verify writes a .received file next to the .verified one whenever a snapshot
## disagrees. It is the failure itself, not a source artifact: committing one
## turns a red test green by replacing the expectation with whatever the code
## just produced. The .verified files ARE versioned — they are the assertion.
*.received.*

## Reqnroll generates a .feature.cs next to each .feature at build time.
## Generated code is a build output: committing it means every build produces a
## diff, and a stale one silently disagrees with its .feature file.
*.feature.cs

## IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

## NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
packages/
!fixtures/**/packages/
!fixtures/**/packages/**

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Preflight's own runtime output. Per-machine, append-only, never versioned.
.preflight/

## Local policy overlay. The developer's own override; CI must never see it.
preflight.local.json

## Local JetBrains Junie folder.
.junie/
